Find the echo's delay when it comes sooner than the delay headroom, and move to it only when the filter cannot reach the echo

With the headroom of 512 samples that patch 0019 of the wrapper sets (8 blocks), an echo
whose delay in the audio processing is shorter than about 34 ms gives lags that the delay
histogram takes as 0 (the lag less the headroom, clamped at 0), and the aggregator of the
highest peak never chooses 0: its 250 slots start filled with lag 0 while its histogram
starts empty, so bin 0 starts 250 down and never reaches the thresholds. No delay is ever
found, and the echo controller stays where its reset put it (with a reported delay R, R/4
- 2 blocks; without one, 5 blocks). When the echo comes before that, out of the linear
filter's reach, the filter never becomes usable: the transparent mode takes it for a
headset after about 8 s and lets the echo through at 0 dB for the rest of the call.
Measured in the AEC3 simulator (M158 with main's patches, 16 kHz, echo of speech at 0 dB):
with a reported delay of 30 ms and an echo of 5 to 11 ms, 50 ms and 5 to 30 ms, or none
and 5 to 10 ms; through a room's response at 50 ms and 5 to 10 ms, -7 to -10 dB.

The aggregator now also follows the lags shorter than the headroom. When it finds no
delay and its latest 125 lags all came that short and within 2 of each other, it gives a
delay of 0. The controller moves the buffer to it only when the last such lag puts the
echo before where the buffer stands; where the filter still reaches the echo, the buffer
stays and the filter keeps what it learned. The aggregator's own histogram is left as it
is: letting its bin 0 win (the slots not yet written marked as such, as the pre-echo
aggregator does) also took the short lags that music gives now and then, and moved the
buffer with music on speakers (one half second up to 24 dB more echo); so did 25 or 50
lags in a row.

Simulator, same cases: the echo is cancelled to -57 dB all the call (room: -43 to -45 dB,
as with longer delays). Identical: echo of 20 to 400 ms, the start of a call with music or
speech on speakers (echo -10 to -30 dB, also with the near end talking) or on a headset,
double talk with music or speech (16 seeds each). The unmute series (48 seeds, echo of 30
ms with no reported delay, and 60 ms reported 50) changes in 5 seeds, each with less echo.
After an unmute (2 s muted) with an echo of 5 to 20 ms and a reported 30 to 50 ms, the
echo after the first second goes from -15 to +6 dB to -25 to -37 dB; the first second, while
the buffer moves, is at -6 to -11 dB (before: 0 dB with a single echo, -12 to -43 dB with
a room's). Through a room's response, 2 runs of 48 (reported 30 ms, echo 15 and 20 ms) that
were cancelled before now have one burst at -13 and -17 dB.

